    "result_text": "The full suite passes \u2014 there is a single test class and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-match \"possible duplicate\" rule for owner creation. When a new owner is created and isn't a hard (identity) duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, it's still created and now reports `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matched owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nChanges, each kept in the unit where it belongs:\n\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 two new persisted columns (`possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`) with getters/setters, so the flags survive to the later `GET /api/owners/{id}` the test reads them back from.\n- **`PossibleDuplicateMatcher.java`** (new) \u2014 single responsibility: given the candidate, find the earliest-created stored owner sharing last name (case-insensitive) and postcode with a different telephone. Owners without a postcode never match. Mirrors the existing `HouseholdMatcher`/`NamesakeCounter` style and reuses `ClinicService`.\n- **`PossibleDuplicateAssigner.java`** (new) \u2014 thin assigner that delegates to the matcher and sets the two fields, matching the existing `*Assigner` convention.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 wired the assigner into the create pipeline just before save (after the identity-duplicate guard, so it only runs for owners that are actually created), injected via the constructor like the other collaborators.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32) as read-only fields on the `Owner` schema; MapStruct maps them automatically by name.\n- **`schema.sql`** (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added the `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` and the full suite build green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).",
